//? Title: Gauss–Legendre π: quadratic mathematics, fixed-precision limits
//? Subtitle: Actual AGM states, a two-ULP plateau, disappearing corrections and honest reference errors
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Compute π rapidly while tracking how arithmetic precision limits the result.
A fast-converging formula can still stagnate at a value that is not correctly
rounded. The Gauss–Legendre iteration combines arithmetic and geometric means
with a correction accumulator. This report follows an actual first step, reruns
the original six-step example and separates reference differences from error
against mathematical π. Native snapshots show that the estimate stalls before
the means do, while the means themselves eventually remain one ULP apart.
Work counters and explicit record/domain limits expose what further fixed-count
iterations actually do.
)

\toc

> Start with one arithmetic mean, one geometric mean and a correction

Initialize a=1, b=1/sqrt(2), t=1/4 and p=1. The arithmetic mean of a and b is
about 0.853553; the geometric mean is about 0.840896. Use the old a and its new
arithmetic mean to update t, then double p. The diagram reads these values from
the first actual native record, including the correction used by the kernel.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/legendre_first.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gauss_legendre_pi.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_trace(1);const auto&e=t.steps.at(0);
 std::print("| state | a | b | t | p |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Before | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.1f} |\n| After | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} | {:.1f} |\n",e.before.a,e.before.b,e.before.t,e.before.p,e.after.a,e.after.b,e.after.t,e.after.p);
 std::print("\nActual correction {:.12g}; estimate {:.17g}; square roots {}; captured records {}.\n",e.correction,e.estimate,t.run.work.square_roots,t.captured_records);
 dm::graphics::Diagram d(63,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.4;box.height=2.4;box.font_size=21;
 d.node("start",{0,0},std::format("Actual starting state\na = {:.6f}\nb = {:.6f}\nt = {:.2f}, p = {:.0f}",e.before.a,e.before.b,e.before.t,e.before.p),box)
  .node("means",{6,0},std::format("Two different means\na next = {:.6f}\nb next = {:.6f}",e.after.a,e.after.b),box)
  .node("correct",{12,0},std::format("Apply used correction\nt = {:.6f}, p = {:.0f}\nestimate = {:.9f}",e.after.t,e.after.p,e.estimate),box)
  .edge("start","means","average").edge("means","correct","correct t")
  .text({6,2.5},"AGM states contract; the correction connects the limit to pi",26).save_svg("build/legendre_first.svg");
 if(e.iteration!=1||!e.estimate_changed||t.steps.size()!=1)throw std::runtime_error("first actual stage");
}
