\caption(The original one-, two- and three-step estimates are preserved. Later double estimates stay two reference ULPs above the nearest double π, so they are not correctly rounded π.)
\alttext(Two reference-error curves drop from about10^-3 to10^-8 and then near10^-15, with a nonzero plateau. The table distinguishes double and wider references and reports the two-ULP offset.)

The old report's “last bit” claim is contradicted by the actual result: the plateau
is two ULPs above the nearest double π, where one ULP here is the spacing at that
reference. It is also an approximation to an exact-arithmetic lower formula that
rounding can move above π. Such computed values are not certified brackets.
A first unchanged estimate only says that two computed estimates compare equal.
Extra iterations of the same rounded recurrence do not repair past rounding.

> A nonzero correction can disappear when t is stored

At stage 4, the used correction is positive but too small to change the rounded t.
The means still change at that stage. At stage 5, a, b and t all stop changing,
yet a and b remain distinct, one double ULP apart. The doubling weight p continues
to change, so it is intentionally excluded from the mean-state stagnation flag.
Neither flag asserts mathematical convergence. The following record table also
separates the used correction from the rounded difference t_before-t_after.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/legendre_states.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gauss_legendre_pi.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 const auto t=dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_trace(8);std::vector<double>xgap,gap_y,xcorr,corr_y;
 std::print("| stage | a-b after | used correction | rounded t difference | estimate changed | (a,b,t) changed |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
 for(const auto&e:t.steps){const double gap=e.after.a-e.after.b;std::print("| {} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {:.6e} | {} | {} |\n",e.iteration,gap,e.correction,e.before.t-e.after.t,e.estimate_changed,e.mean_state_changed);if(gap>0){xgap.push_back(e.iteration);gap_y.push_back(std::log10(gap));}if(e.correction>0){xcorr.push_back(e.iteration);corr_y.push_back(std::log10(e.correction));}}
 std::print("\nFinal a {:.17g}; b {:.17g}; equal {}; first unchanged estimate {}; first unchanged mean state {}.\n",t.run.final.a,t.run.final.b,t.run.final.a==t.run.final.b,t.run.first_unchanged_estimate,t.run.first_unchanged_mean_state);
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(xgap,gap_y,"Mean gap",{37,99,235},2).points(xgap,gap_y,"",{37,99,235},4)
  .lines(xcorr,corr_y,"Used correction",{220,38,38},2).points(xcorr,corr_y,"",{220,38,38},4).legend({"Mean gap","Used correction"},{{37,99,235},{220,38,38}})
  .title("Rounded mean states can stall with a nonzero gap").xlab("Actual stage").ylab("log10 positive mean gap or positive used correction").y_limits(-23,1).size(1100,540).save_svg("build/legendre_states.svg");
 if(t.steps[3].correction<=0||t.steps[3].before.t!=t.steps[3].after.t||t.run.final.a==t.run.final.b)throw std::runtime_error("lost correction and nonzero gap");
}
