> Requested fixed-precision work still grows linearly

For N admitted stages, the shared recurrence executes N arithmetic means,
N geometric means, N correction updates and N weight doublings. Including
initialization, it uses N+1 square roots. The analysis APIs evaluate N+1 estimates
to detect changes, whereas the legacy scalar API evaluates only the final
estimate expression. No API stops early merely because an estimate or mean
state stagnates. Ordinary analysis uses O(N) arithmetic and O(1) result storage;
owned fixed-schema histories use O(N) records and copying.

This operation count differs from the complexity of obtaining more mathematical
digits with variable precision. Brent's discussion on printed 247 requires guard
bits and gives O(M(n)log n) cost for n-bit π using n-bit multiplication cost M(n).
It also notes that AGM is not self-correcting. Quadratic exact convergence cannot
create millions of digits inside a fixed double; arithmetic precision must grow.
The following plot counts actual square-root evaluations, not elapsed time.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/legendre_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/gauss_legendre_pi.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <array>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numbers>
#include <print>
namespace dm=datamunge;
int main(){
 std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
 std::vector<double>x,y;
 std::print("| requested stages | square roots | mean pairs | correction updates | weight updates | analysis estimate evaluations | trace records needed | final weight finite |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
 for(int n:std::array<int,13>{0,1,2,3,4,5,6,8,16,64,256,dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_limit()-1,dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_limit()}){const auto s=dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_run(n);std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,s.work.square_roots,s.work.arithmetic_means,s.work.correction_updates,s.work.power_updates,s.work.estimate_evaluations,dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_trace_records(n),std::isfinite(s.final.p));if(n>0){x.push_back(std::log2(double(n)));y.push_back(std::log2(double(s.work.square_roots)));}if(s.work.square_roots!=n+1||s.work.power_updates!=n)throw std::runtime_error("fixed-count work");}
 auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();plot.lines(x,y,"Actual square roots",{37,99,235},2).points(x,y,"",{37,99,235},4)
  .title("More requested fixed-precision stages still perform more work").xlab("log2 requested positive stage count").ylab("log2 actual square-root evaluations, including initialization").y_limits(0,12).size(1100,540).save_svg("build/legendre_work.svg");
 std::print("\nSafe used-weight limit {}; the last unused doubling may overflow; estimate remains finite {}.\n",dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_limit(),std::isfinite(dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi(dm::algorithms::gauss_legendre_pi_limit())));
}
