\caption(Exact record admission is 7 for six stages. The zero-height reference-offset bar means equality to the rounded double reference; the wider-reference column explains why that is not exact mathematical π.)
\alttext(Two panels show record counts7,7 and rejected 6, then ULP offsets2 for the native plateau and0 for rounded pi. Computed log flags and domain controls accompany the figure.)

Actual states, counters and unclipped reference differences preserve the original
calculation while correcting its accuracy interpretation. Quadratic mathematics
explains the rapid initial improvement; finite precision explains the plateau,
disappearing corrections and the gap between equality tests and mathematical
convergence. These generated constant-iteration states need no external dataset.
